# ACL of the Mosquitto of the OEC dev environment (oec/dev, C-071).
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY. MG 9.1 (REQ-GEN-001): only authorized clients may send
# Set, Del and Call requests; Set/Config should not be readable by others
# (REQ-RES-CONFIG-026). Mosquitto checks every PUBLISH against this file and
# drops (and acknowledges) a denied one; a denied subscription gets 0x80.
#
# Limitation of the dev environment: Mosquitto cannot bind the AppId topic
# level (base64url of the Identification Link) to a user, so every client
# may read Oi4v2/# – including the Set/Config of other applications, which
# an application needs for its own Set/Config. `oec-infra bus` therefore
# warns on REQ-RES-CONFIG-026 against oec/dev (C-071 log).

# The probe user of the test tools (oec-check test, interop probe,
# oec-infra bus) is privileged: it requests Set, Del and Call.
user oec-probe
topic readwrite #

# Every client (pattern lines apply to all users, also oec-probe): read the
# Message Bus, publish Pub (answers, data, Health, MAM, Event, Will), Get and
# Reply (the answer to a Call, MG 9.2).
pattern read Oi4v2/#
pattern write Oi4v2/+/+/Pub/#
pattern write Oi4v2/+/+/Get/#
pattern write Oi4v2/+/+/Reply/#
